# Python bytecode from running merge-settings.py or its fixture. A .pyc embeds
# the absolute path it was compiled from, so committing one under this subtree
# would publish a path from whatever machine happened to build it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The retired host companion of the Ensemble's settings.json, and the copies
# the deploy leaves when it retires one (settings.local.json.retired-<timestamp>).
# Both carry machine paths. deploy-to-host.{ps1,sh} still reads a
# settings.local.json it finds here, once, to move its values into the config
# home's own settings.json, and then renames it rather than deleting it, so the
# file and its renamed copies can sit in this folder. One pattern keeps them all
# untracked. Host values now live in the config home's settings.json;
# settings.optout.example.md describes them.
/settings.local.json*
